This page documents the backup process for GitLab and Nexus configuration files in Prod Environment, including encryption, S3 upload, replication validation, and decryption steps.



Overview
GitLab and Nexus configuration backups are automated using shell scripts that:

Package configuration files into a .tar.gz archive

Encrypt the archive using OpenSSL AES‑256‑CBC

Upload the encrypted file to Amazon S3

Support cross‑region replication (CRR)

Allow secure restoration using AWS Secrets Manager



