5. Backup Workflow
1	Collect GitLab/Nexus configuration files
2	Create a .tar.gz archive containing the configuration backup
3	Retrieve encryption password securely from AWS Secrets Manager
4	Encrypt the archive using OpenSSL with the retrieved password
5	Upload the encrypted .enc file to the S3 bucket
6	Cross‑Region Replication (CRR) automatically copies the encrypted file to the DR region
7	Use the decrypt script to download, decrypt, and extract the backup when needed
6. Restore / Decrypt Backup
6.1 Run Decrypt Script


./decrypt_s3_file.sh s3://s3-crr-frankfurt/frankfurt-config/gitlab-node-backups/<file>.enc

The script will:

Download encrypted file

Fetch password from Secrets Manager

Decrypt using OpenSSL

Extract the archive

