All gitlab.rb configurations are version-controlled in Git and updated through feature branches and merge requests. Once approved and merged into the main branch, a CI/CD pipeline automatically deploys the changes using Ansible to the appropriate GitLab nodes (Rails, Gitaly, and Praefect). This ensures consistent, auditable, and automated configuration management across the GitLab infrastructure.

Note- Ansible is already installed on Prod 142 server & Test 140 server. So to implement this we have to register a gitlab runner in same nodes.

Deployment Procedure
Create Change

Create a feature branch from main

Update:

Node-specific template (rails.rb.j2, gitaly.rb.j2, praefect.rb.j2)

Corresponding variables in group_vars

Submit for Review

Open a Merge Request (MR) targeting main

Ensure required reviewers approve the change

Merge Change

Merge the MR after approval

Do not squash or bypass review controls

Pipeline Execution

GitLab CI/CD pipeline triggers automatically on merge 

Pipeline runs:
 
ansible-playbook -i inventory/production playbooks/deploy.yml

Configuration Deployment

Ansible selects the correct template based on host group

Renders and copies gitlab.rb to /etc/gitlab/gitlab.rb

Apply Configuration

Handler executes:

gitlab-ctl reconfigure

Configuration is applied on affected nodes

